{
  "behaviorChanges": [
    "The default blocking graphify freshness gate is now the dependency-free no-LLM AST refresh. `graphify.updateCommand` and `graphify.buildCommand` both default to `graphify update .` instead of the retired auto-detect forms (a bare `graphify .` invocation, with and without an update flag), and `graphify.freshnessRule` states that LLM-backed graphify invocations are never the blocking gate. A lane on defaults changes behavior automatically and its commit/push gate can no longer be broken by a third party retiring an auto-detected model. A lane that pinned the old command in adapter JSON keeps its pin and should adopt the split (see optionalMigrations).",
    "Two new adapter keys are REQUIRED non-blank and published in `methodology/adapter-schema.json`: `graphify.semanticCommand` (default `GRAPHIFY_CLAUDE_CLI_MODEL=haiku graphify label . --backend=claude-cli`) and `graphify.semanticRule`. Adapters that omit them inherit the defaults and keep validating, because defaults merge under adapter values before validation; only an adapter that sets one of them BLANK is refused. They nest inside the open `properties.graphify` sub-schema, so a pre-push schema check by an older installed runtime does not refuse them.",
    "The gate's remediation strings are read from adapter config instead of hardcoded. `graphify-status`, the generated git hooks, and the rendered adapter's Graphify Navigation bullet now print the CONFIGURED `graphify.updateCommand` and `graphify.buildCommand`, so a project that overrides them is no longer told to run a command it does not use. The rendered bullet's `(no-LLM)` qualifier is attached only when the configured command IS the no-LLM default, so an adapter that pins an LLM-backed invocation is never handed a generated file claiming otherwise. Output that pinned the old literal changes text."
  ],
